WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:07.646
A venue needs a team for Friday. A manager
needs to know who's booked. And staff need

2
00:00:07.646 --> 00:00:10.805
to know where to be, and what happens
next.

3
00:00:11.505 --> 00:00:16.774
Crewflow connects that whole journey, from
the first request to the final timesheet.

4
00:00:22.074 --> 00:00:27.088
Managers run their agency from the web
console. Each manager has a private

5
00:00:27.088 --> 00:00:30.543
workspace, with their own staff, venues
and shifts.

6
00:00:31.143 --> 00:00:36.301
Venue managers use the Crewflow app to
request staff. Staff use the same app to

7
00:00:36.301 --> 00:00:39.566
see their offers, clock in, and check
their hours.

8
00:00:42.466 --> 00:00:47.346
It starts with the team. In the web
console, the manager keeps a record for

9
00:00:47.346 --> 00:00:49.624
every staff member and every venue.

10
00:00:50.224 --> 00:00:55.251
Each venue manager is linked to a venue,
and the manager decides which staff each

11
00:00:55.251 --> 00:00:56.368
one can work with.

12
00:00:56.868 --> 00:01:00.857
Here, Riley Chen is the venue manager at
Riverside House.

13
00:01:01.357 --> 00:01:05.581
In the app, Riley sees that assigned team,
and no one else.

14
00:01:08.881 --> 00:01:13.870
On Tuesday, Riley needs four waiting staff
for a wedding reception on Friday.

15
00:01:14.370 --> 00:01:19.932
Riley chooses the venue, the role, the
time and the break, then picks four people

16
00:01:19.932 --> 00:01:20.893
from the team.

17
00:01:22.093 --> 00:01:27.224
If someone isn't normally available that
day, Crewflow warns Riley before anything

18
00:01:27.224 --> 00:01:27.725
is sent.

19
00:01:28.325 --> 00:01:33.173
The request goes to the manager for
approval. Nothing reaches the staff yet.

20
00:01:33.873 --> 00:01:39.223
In Venue Offers, the manager checks the
request, adds or removes people if needed,

21
00:01:39.223 --> 00:01:40.267
and approves it.

22
00:01:43.767 --> 00:01:48.839
Approval sends each person their own
offer, with the venue, the time, and their

23
00:01:48.839 --> 00:01:49.738
estimated pay.

24
00:01:50.338 --> 00:01:55.620
Priya opens hers and accepts. Because this
shift came from an approved request, she's

25
00:01:55.620 --> 00:01:56.925
booked straight away.

26
00:01:58.425 --> 00:02:03.685
It's different when the manager creates a
shift directly. Then, accepting holds the

27
00:02:03.685 --> 00:02:05.967
place until the manager confirms it.

28
00:02:06.567 --> 00:02:11.402
Either way, the manager can follow every
person on the staffing board in Venue

29
00:02:11.402 --> 00:02:11.836
Offers.

30
00:02:14.736 --> 00:02:20.155
On Friday, Priya's confirmed shift is
waiting in her app. Clock-in opens shortly

31
00:02:20.155 --> 00:02:21.307
before it starts.

32
00:02:21.907 --> 00:02:26.835
At the venue, she scans the shift's QR
code, and Crewflow's server checks it.

33
00:02:27.635 --> 00:02:30.781
Some venues also require her to be on
site.

34
00:02:31.381 --> 00:02:35.960
Her shift is now live, timed by Crewflow's
own clock, not her phone's.

35
00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:41.815
When the shift ends, she scans the same
code again to clock out.

36
00:02:44.715 --> 00:02:47.668
Afterwards, Riley opens the shift report.

37
00:02:48.168 --> 00:02:52.968
Three people clocked in and out. Isla
clocked in, but never clocked out, so

38
00:02:52.968 --> 00:02:57.256
Crewflow flags the missing clock-out
instead of guessing her hours.

39
00:02:57.856 --> 00:03:02.305
Riley enters the right time, gives a
reason, and saves the correction.

40
00:03:03.905 --> 00:03:09.116
Saving a correction doesn't approve it.
Riley still marks each person's hours as

41
00:03:09.116 --> 00:03:10.484
reviewed, one by one.

42
00:03:12.284 --> 00:03:16.037
Rating each person's work is a separate,
optional step.

43
00:03:16.637 --> 00:03:21.431
Finalise & send only unlocks once everyone
is clocked out and reviewed.

44
00:03:24.731 --> 00:03:30.458
Riley confirms the break details, signs
off by typing a full name, and sends. That

45
00:03:30.458 --> 00:03:31.575
locks the hours.

46
00:03:32.775 --> 00:03:37.951
Crewflow then creates the final timesheet
as a PDF, queues it for delivery, and

47
00:03:37.951 --> 00:03:39.655
shows when it's been sent.

48
00:03:41.455 --> 00:03:44.372
In the app, the finished shift moves to
History.

49
00:03:44.872 --> 00:03:49.410
In the web console, the manager can open
both the original and the signed

50
00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:50.032
timesheet.

51
00:03:52.932 --> 00:03:57.965
Back in the web console, the hours appear
in Payroll, with the pay they add up to.

52
00:03:57.965 --> 00:03:59.929
Crewflow doesn't move any money.

53
00:04:00.529 --> 00:04:04.860
Ratings from venue managers build up on
each staff member's record.

54
00:04:05.460 --> 00:04:10.583
And the dashboard and calendar show the
week ahead, the hours worked, and how

55
00:04:10.583 --> 00:04:12.180
ready the next shift is.

56
00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:21.292
Behind the scenes, the web console and the
app share one Crewflow service. On every

57
00:04:21.292 --> 00:04:25.437
request, it checks who you are, and which
workspace you belong to.

58
00:04:26.037 --> 00:04:30.261
Background jobs look after reminders,
expiries and documents.

59
00:04:33.161 --> 00:04:37.308
Request. Approve. Work. Review. Sign off.
That's Crewflow.

60
00:04:39.308 --> 00:04:42.671
To get started, open the guide for your
role.
